# candidate T20 Change 6 -- TWO-PRIME bounded fused dot
#   One operand of the Ajtai product is G^-1(m), whose coefficients are
#   unsigned gadget digits (< GADGET_BASE = 16). The exact convolution
#   then fits p1*p2 = 4.69e17 rather than needing p1*p2*p3, so the
#   per-term work drops from 3 x 7168 to 2 x 7168 modular multiplies:
#   a twist (1024), a forward transform (5120) and a pointwise MAC
#   (1024) per prime. Predicted -33% of the dot, ~-22% of the caller.
# BOUND_D = N * 16 * Q = 2^46 (still a multiple of Q, so invisible mod Q).
#   2*L*BOUND_D < p1*p2 gives L <= 3332; DOT_CHUNK_D = 2048 is the
#   largest power of two below that, so 4 chunks at the 8192 width.
# NOT applied to the balanced path: centred digits give a two-sided word
#   bound (< 8 or > q-9), for which this argument does not hold.
# hachi/src is the CHAMPION for this run and is not touched until the
#   report lands -- run 6 of Change 4 was lost exactly that way.
